    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 14).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, every Python file is represented by **two coexisting Symbol nodes** of different kinds: one `kind=\"file\"` and one `kind=\"module\"`. Only the file-kind node carries edges; the module-kind node sits orphan.\n\n**Concrete case** for `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py` (3179 lines):\n\n```\nNode 1 (kind=file):\n  origin: orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis\n  name:   /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py  (absolute, broken — see R14-A)\n  span:   1-1                                                                                       (broken — see R14-A)\n  edges as src: 60\n  edges as dst: 0\n\nNode 2 (kind=module):\n  origin: python-ast-v1\n  name:   <module:cli.py>           (clean)\n  span:   1-3179                    (correct)\n  edges as src: 0\n  edges as dst: 0\n```\n\n**Scale on self-analysis.** Out of all Python files:\n\n| Pattern | Path count |\n|---|---:|\n| Both `file` AND `module` kind | **332** |\n| `file` kind only | 466 |\n| `module` kind only | 4 |\n\nThe 332 \"both\" group is the redundant representation. 466 \"file-only\" and 4 \"module-only\" suggest the producer rules are inconsistent in their own right — synthesis fires for some files but not others, and python-ast-v1 emits module-kind for some files but not others.\n\n**Adjacent symptom: module-kind nodes are structurally orphan.** Of 385 total module-kind Symbol nodes:\n\n- Only **558 of 18,022 `contains` edges** have a module-kind node as `src` (3.1%)\n- The remaining 17,464 contains edges are class→method\n- There are essentially **no `contains` edges of the form module→function or module→class**\n\nSo even when a file does get a module-kind Symbol, that Symbol doesn't participate in the containment hierarchy. A consumer asking \"what does module X contain?\" gets no useful answer.\n\n**Why this is a problem.**\n\n1. **Duplicate representation breaks `total_files`-style counts** (extends WI-soraj). 332 paths are double-counted by anything iterating Symbols by path-and-kind.\n\n2. **The file/module split is implicit, undocumented, and inconsistently emitted.** Consumers don't know that the two kinds may both exist for the same Python file, or which one to query for \"the canonical file node.\"\n\n3. **Containment graph is broken at the module level.** The natural query \"what top-level functions does cli.py define?\" can't be answered by traversing `contains` from the file-kind or module-kind node. Class-internal containment works fine, but the file/module → top-level-symbol layer is missing.\n\n4. **Module-kind nodes are 100% disconnected** in the 332 file+module pair cases. They take wire-format space and add to the node count, but contribute zero structural information.\n\n**Invariant statement.** For each source file analyzed by the Python analyzer, exactly one canonical Symbol must represent that file in the behavior map (whether `kind=\"file\"` or `kind=\"module\"` is a design choice — but it must be exactly one). The chosen representative Symbol must be the source of `contains` edges to every top-level function, class, and module-level variable defined in that file.\n\n**Severity.** Medium. Affects 332 paths (40% of Python files). Compounds with R14-A (broken synthesizer fields).\n\n**Fix proposal — two viable approaches.**\n\n1. **Choose module as canonical; suppress file-kind synthesis for python.** Remove `orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis`'s file-kind output when a python-ast-v1 module-kind node already exists for the same path. Then re-route any downstream edges that currently point at the file-kind node to point at the module-kind node instead. Add `module→{top-level function, class, variable}` contains edges. Clean fix; requires a sweep of edge consumers.\n\n2. **Choose file as canonical; drop module-kind from python-ast-v1.** Remove module-kind emission from the python analyzer. Keep `orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis`'s file-kind nodes (after fixing R14-A's bugs). Fix containment to emit `file→{top-level symbols}`. Less invasive on the linker side; requires a span/name correction on the synthesizer.\n\nRecommended: **2** for Python (file-kind is what existing linkers reference, leaving them stable) plus the R14-A fixes. (1) would be cleaner conceptually but cascades through all edge consumers.\n\nEither way, the post-fix state should be:\n- One canonical kind per file\n- That node participates in `contains` edges to its top-level children\n- The other kind isn't emitted\n\n**Test gap.** Property test: `len({n.kind for n in nodes if n.path == X and n.language == \"python\"}) == 1` for every path X. Currently 332 violations.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py` — module-kind emission\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/analyze/base.py:375-385` — file-kind synthesis (R14-A's site)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/containment.py` — needs module-level containment rules\n- `R14-A (INV-...)` — same producer as the file-kind side of this; the synthesizer's misbehavior compounds the redundancy\n- `WI-fozoh-...` (done) — EXTERNAL boundary file duplication; INTERNAL file-kind/module-kind redundancy here is a distinct mechanism (different scope, different producers)\n- `INV-ronuf-...` (filed round 6) — linker creates phantom file Symbols; sibling \"redundant file representation\" pattern\n- `WI-soraj-...` (filed round 8) — `total_files` ambiguity; this finding makes the ambiguity worse (double-counting Python files)"  # af97
    fields:  # af97
      statement: "For each source file analyzed by the Python analyzer, exactly one canonical Symbol must represent that file in the behavior map (file-kind or module-kind, by design choice). That canonical Symbol must be the source of 'contains' edges to every top-level function, class, and module-level variable defined in that file."  # af97
      root_cause: "Two producers emit Symbols for the same Python file: (1) orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis emits kind=file (analyze/base.py:375-385); (2) python-ast-v1 emits kind=module. The two coexist without coordination. On self-analysis: 332 paths have both kinds, 466 have file-only, 4 have module-only. Containment-linker only emits class->method edges (17464 of 18022); module->function and module->class containment edges are missing, leaving module-kind nodes structurally orphan even when they exist."  # af97
